sequenceDiagram
    actor User as Operator or CI job
    participant CS as ConfigSyncSubcommand
    participant CFG as deployment files<br/>(~/.baas/deployments/*.yaml)
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation

    Note over User,CF: baas --deployment <prefix> config sync -- operator credentials suffice<br/>(OperatorRole holds cloudformation:DescribeStacks on its own stack only).<br/>Never derived: with nothing configured the name is required, or a bare sync would adopt<br/>whatever deployment the active credentials imply. With exactly one configured, a bare sync re-syncs it.
    User->>CS: baas --deployment baas-123456789012 config sync
    CS->>CFG: loadForSync() -- migrates a flat config.yaml first
    alt no --deployment, and none or 2+ configured
        CS-->>User: name the deployment (the configured ones listed) -- exit 2, nothing written
    end
    Note over CS: the named deployment's file, or a new one -- or the only configured one
    opt no aws.operatorProfile and no ambient credentials
        CS-->>User: warn: using the default credential chain
    end
    CS->>S3: HeadBucket(<prefix>) from any region -- the file's, AWS_REGION or the default
    Note over CS,S3: bucket names are global: a wrong-region request answers 301/400<br/>with x-amz-bucket-region, and a 404 means no bucket (U22)
    alt no bucket
        CS-->>User: "No deployment named ... no bucket of that name" -- exit 1, file untouched
    end
    CS->>CF: DescribeStacks(<prefix>) in the bucket's region, operator credentials
    alt stack absent
        CF-->>CS: does not exist
        CS-->>User: a bucket but no stack -- nothing to adopt -- exit 1, file untouched
    else stack present
        CF-->>CS: outputs
        opt no ResultsTableName output
            CS-->>User: warn: stack predates the results table
        end
        Note over CS: Outputs are read to prove existence only -- nothing is copied.<br/>Bucket, table, profile, pointer are derived from the prefix --<br/>subnet + security group are resolved per job.
        CS->>CFG: save deployments/<prefix>.yaml -- prefix AND aws.region (the deployment's)
        CS-->>User: Adopted <prefix> in <region> -- bucket, table -- exit 0
    end
